#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147148 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147575 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb8b97e4-704c-5b13-97c7-6eb97aca392f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Multiple of Ten Percent"}] :question/id #uuid "e650884c-e858-5213-8ff4-a39f9358edc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-13066" :question/problem "If ![](images/18/18d57a5f075275e8b44ff372bbccb5677682ab13c3d316030da5410ab62343ad.svg) then what is the missing number?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the part is $36,$ the percentage is $50\\%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $50\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{50}{100} = \\dfrac{50\\div 50}{100\\div 50} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =36÷50% \\\\  & =36÷\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =36\\times \\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =36\\times 2 \\\\  & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147149 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147576 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c69dea-ec5d-525d-ae0f-da30e342fe63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage"}] :question/id #uuid "4bfda07b-18fd-541a-a627-ef7f1e47f41a" :question/math-academy-id "e-13067" :question/problem "$34\\%$ of a number is $170.$ What is the number?" :question/worked-solution "We're given that the part is $170,$ the percentage is $34\\%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $34\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{34}{100} = \\dfrac{34\\div 2}{100\\div 2} = \\dfrac{17}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =170÷34% \\\\  & =170÷\\frac{17}{50} \\\\  & =170\\times \\frac{50}{17} \\\\  & =\\frac{170}{17}\\times 50 \\\\  & =10\\times 50 \\\\  & =500\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147150 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147577 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1670b7f6-fdee-5358-b145-9254e2a4ba50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage: Word Problems"}] :question/id #uuid "bd7aaf49-0da5-53c8-a5ee-863523548957" :question/math-academy-id "e-13068" :question/problem "In the math club, there are $16$ girls and some boys. If the girls represent $40\\%$ of the total members of the club, how many members does the math club have?" :question/worked-solution "We're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of girls in the math club, which is $16.$ The percentage is $40\\%,$ and the whole is the total number of club members.\n\nTo find the whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $40\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{40}{100} = \\dfrac{40\\div 20}{100\\div 20} = \\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =16÷40% \\\\  & =16÷\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =16\\times \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2}\\times 5 \\\\  & =8\\times 5 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the club has $40$ members."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147575 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb8b97e4-704c-5b13-97c7-6eb97aca392f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Multiple of Ten Percent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0989f7fd-0593-51f1-ad5d-522251531367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500484} {:answer/id #uuid "487be039-8cee-556f-a591-54683cd090f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500610} {:answer/id #uuid "671b3be1-5da4-5cf9-8892-6dde4b4dacdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500682} {:answer/id #uuid "74d23ef3-2cb1-5f88-a2da-701c7fa11d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500706} {:answer/id #uuid "ae45bd3b-76a6-5d21-9e72-9e93992e481c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74d23ef3-2cb1-5f88-a2da-701c7fa11d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500706} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a60f895-e24e-53bc-9d51-27f66d1ee4cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "706f9bb5-de0a-5c75-aa53-ea495445a284" :question/math-academy-id "q-160355" :question/problem "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 20%=14,$ then $\\,\\boxed{}=$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $14,$ the percentage is $20%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $20%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =14÷20% \\\\  & =14÷\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =14\\times \\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =14\\times 5 \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147576 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c69dea-ec5d-525d-ae0f-da30e342fe63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5e59494-db50-5c09-a591-ffc1049b89d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5e59494-db50-5c09-a591-ffc1049b89d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500808} :answer-field/id #uuid "646d465e-4f31-55a7-9533-68a3a82b8349" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b23ca4fe-ec69-5d5b-b163-9360e0e9626e" :question/math-academy-id "q-171157" :question/problem "$14%$ of{{field-1}}\nis $7.$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $7,$ the percentage is $14%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\n \n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $14%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{100}=\\frac{14÷2}{100÷2}=\\frac{7}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =7÷14% \\\\  & =7÷\\frac{7}{50} \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{50}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7}\\times 50 \\\\  & =1\\times 50 \\\\  & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $14%$ of $50$ is $7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147575 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb8b97e4-704c-5b13-97c7-6eb97aca392f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Multiple of Ten Percent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7203a599-e145-56ae-a118-e1542346dd81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7203a599-e145-56ae-a118-e1542346dd81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500702} :answer-field/id #uuid "5201df42-972e-5151-bdcf-0c219c0c0b6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0060ce0-85fa-5c15-8314-02a2f37da794" :question/math-academy-id "q-185091" :question/problem "What is the missing number?\n\n{{field-1}}$\\times \\,30%=24.$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $24,$ the percentage is $30%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $30%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{100}=\\frac{30÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =24÷30% \\\\  & =24÷\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =24\\times \\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{3}\\times 10 \\\\  & =8\\times 10 \\\\  & =80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $80\\times 30%=24.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147576 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c69dea-ec5d-525d-ae0f-da30e342fe63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c26707e-2356-5432-a9e9-cb0c0034c30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500557} {:answer/id #uuid "472c9925-e5fa-552e-bf38-58b1ee86cb75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1800" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500608} {:answer/id #uuid "a528645b-6270-574c-b026-6e64dc590071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500804} {:answer/id #uuid "cb93aefd-fe15-5f7f-96a3-d16e2cbef808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500899} {:answer/id #uuid "f048a6d4-4633-5a87-b299-018587a58a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f048a6d4-4633-5a87-b299-018587a58a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500977} :answer-field/id #uuid "3afa6d9f-7316-5ca5-8481-6c0db0d97e7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "449615c3-fdfe-5f50-a3b0-a60b4eb31574" :question/math-academy-id "q-61300" :question/problem "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 25%=90,$ then what is the missing number?" :question/worked-solution "The part is $90,$ the percentage is $25%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\n \n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $25%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}=\\frac{25÷25}{100÷25}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =90÷25% \\\\  & =90÷\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =90\\times \\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =90\\times 4 \\\\  & =360\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147577 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1670b7f6-fdee-5358-b145-9254e2a4ba50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae02206-f280-552b-9c7e-f1b25280fec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500488} {:answer/id #uuid "0bc1090e-61d0-5086-8900-d3ac3d3c7142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500492} {:answer/id #uuid "175774cc-bfba-5313-9d4b-4d00fbc5ce0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500520} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3f93d0-753a-5489-8c3f-af8fc22cc58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500829} {:answer/id #uuid "bc1ca7bf-82a2-5e5e-8c98-5cf6337f7731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ae02206-f280-552b-9c7e-f1b25280fec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500488} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4089d0-6e83-5bb9-a01d-10713a8e31b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2281cf7-5deb-5971-96fe-4f78cb0692fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-61343" :question/problem "A school's softball team lost $18%$ of the games they played last year. If the team lost $9$ games last year, how many games did the team win?" :question/worked-solution "We need to know the total number of games played to determine the number of games won. \n\nWe're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of games the team lost, which is $9.$ The percentage is $18%,$ and the whole is the total number of games played. \n\nTo find the whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $18%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{18}{100}=\\frac{18÷2}{100÷2}=\\frac{9}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =9÷18% \\\\  & =9÷\\frac{9}{50} \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{50}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}\\times 50 \\\\  & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played by the softball team last year was $50.$ The total number of games won is\n\n$$\n50-9=41.\n$$\n\nHence, the softball team won $41$ games last year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147577 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1670b7f6-fdee-5358-b145-9254e2a4ba50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aec6150-9598-5e15-864d-cc269bf8d608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500489} {:answer/id #uuid "856414f5-6bd6-5446-a194-c71a91eb1415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500744} {:answer/id #uuid "91fd5ca4-51e8-5656-b5cc-97c65ac29624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500766} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c6e615-7f75-5019-a63a-1a7759574db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500844} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d57cb4-9cbb-5091-b7e4-afb49f54a805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aec6150-9598-5e15-864d-cc269bf8d608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500489} :answer-field/id #uuid "848eb4e6-ce36-56ea-a0f1-8a1fe68b6389" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87c3bda2-8545-5669-83e3-84c3d08222b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-61346" :question/problem "On a math test, Kevin answered $95%$ of the problems correctly. If he answered $38$ problems correctly, how many problems were on the test?" :question/worked-solution "We're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of problems answered correctly, which is $38.$ The percentage is $95%,$ and the whole is the total number of problems on the test. \n\nTo solve this question, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $95%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{95}{100}=\\frac{95÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{19}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =38÷95% \\\\  & =38÷\\frac{19}{20} \\\\  & =38\\times \\frac{20}{19} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{19}\\times 20 \\\\  & =2\\times 20 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there were $40$ problems on the test."}]}
